namespace SandboxAPI

import jo.IO.stdout
import harpe.caps.*
import harpe.caps.drawing.*

// The agent's contract: the entry point the LLM implements each turn, and the
// capabilities it receives. Grant more by declaring capability params and widening
// `receives`; the implementations are built in the runtime, the LLM only gets the
// capability.

// The capability params (`fs`, the format backends, `image`, `ocr`, `graphics`)
// are the standard ones declared in the caps module — an agent only widens
// `receives` here. `fs` is the agent's data directory (`data/`) as a confined,
// read-only tree; its openPDF/openWorkbook/openWord shortcuts go through the
// pdfReader/excelReader/wordReader backend params, which the runtime binds (and a
// custom runtime may rebind). `graphics` draws raster images (diagrams, charts)
// and saves them under the data root.
defer def runTask(): Unit receives stdout, fs, pdfReader, excelReader, wordReader, excelWriter, wordWriter, pdfWriter, image, ocr, graphics
